# ─── Paths ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Absolute path to the brain/content directory where all data is stored.
# Default: ../../brain/content  (relative to backend/, resolves to repo root)
# Set this only if you want to keep data outside the repo.
# VAULT_PATH=/absolute/path/to/brain/content

# Working directory for the terminal opened via the console button in the UI.
# Default: repo root (two levels above backend/)
# WORK_DIR=/absolute/path/to/repo

# ─── Server ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Port the backend listens on.
# Default: 3001
# PORT=3001

# ─── Local AI runtime ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The app never stores provider keys. Authenticate the CLI locally, then choose
# one runtime. `none` preserves every non-AI Life OS feature.
AI_RUNTIME=none

# Codex: sign in with `codex` before selecting this runtime.
# CODEX_COMMAND=codex
# CODEX_MODEL=

# OpenCode: Life OS talks only to a user-managed local `opencode serve`.
# Start it explicitly (without --auto) on the same fixed endpoint:
# `opencode serve --hostname 127.0.0.1 --port 4096`.
# Provider credentials stay in OpenCode's own config/auth — never put them here.
# The default server URL is http://127.0.0.1:4096 and must remain loopback-only.
# OPENCODE_COMMAND=opencode
# The Life OS setup/chat session bridge intentionally uses this exact model.
# OPENCODE_MODEL=assistant/assistant
# OPENCODE_SERVER_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4096

# Origins allowed to issue an explicit terminal-launch click in Life OS.
# Comma-separated only when the Vite UI is deliberately hosted elsewhere.
# LIFE_OS_UI_ORIGIN=http://localhost:5173

# ─── Google Calendar (optional) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Enables two-way sync with Google Calendar.
# Setup: https://console.cloud.google.com → Create project → Enable Calendar API
#        → OAuth 2.0 credentials → Desktop app
#
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=...apps.googleusercontent.com
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=GOCSPX-...
# GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:3001/api/sync/auth/callback
# GOOGLE_TIMEZONE=Europe/Moscow
